Apple has apparently listened to user feedback and brought back the App Switcher screen in the latest watchOS 27.2 beta, but accessing it is a little different than before.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/02/apple-watch-app-switcher.jpeg" alt="watch" width="1920" height="1080" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1036616" /><br/>
In watchOS 26 and earlier versions, a double press of the Digital Crown would bring up the App Switcher, where you could easily switch to the last-used app and view and open other recently used apps. You could also swipe left on a misbehaving app to force close it. <br/>
<br/>
In watchOS 27, the Digital Crown double-press gesture is now reserved for Apple's upcoming new <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/10/apple-watch-live-rewind/">Live Rewind</a> AI feature, so it no longer brings up the App Switcher screen. There were <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/17/watchos-27-removes-useful-apple-watch-feature/">concerns</a> that this meant the App Switcher would be gone for good, but Apple has reinstated it in the second watchOS 27.2 beta, released <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/21/apple-releases-watchos-27-2-beta-2/">yesterday</a>. <br/>
<br/>
The gesture for opening it has changed, though.<br/>
<br/>
As shown in the video below, you now access the App Switcher by pressing and holding the bottom of the screen while you're in an app.<br/>
